# Example crontab entry for a periodic full-repo security sweep — the "deep
# scan on a schedule" half of the layered trigger model (see
# docs/architecture.md). This runs the more expensive scan-full (LLM review
# + SCA dependency scan) less often than the per-PR scan-diff, by design.
#
# Install with `crontab -e`, then paste a line like the one below after
# editing the paths and OWNER/REPO. This example runs daily at 3am.
#
# cron runs with a minimal environment (no shell profile), so this sources
# a .env file explicitly rather than assuming ANTHROPIC_API_KEY/GITHUB_TOKEN
# are already set.
#
# For a more robust setup on a long-lived server (auto-restart on failure,
# structured logging via journald, dependency ordering), a systemd timer +
# service pair is the usual upgrade path from cron. Not included here to
# keep this example minimal — the crontab line below is equivalent for a
# single-machine setup, which is all Phase 1 needs.

0 3 * * * cd /path/to/target/repo && /usr/bin/env bash -c 'set -a; source /path/to/autonomous-software-maintenance-agent/.env; set +a; exec /path/to/autonomous-software-maintenance-agent/.venv/bin/maintenance-agent scan-full --repo . --github-repo OWNER/REPO' >> /var/log/maintenance-agent-full-scan.log 2>&1
